NameError 'True' is not declared — V2 writes true
NameError 'None' is not declared — V2 writes null
NameError 'undefined' is not declared — V2 writes null
NameError 'console' is not declared — V2 prints with print(...)
TypeError list has no method 'append' — did you mean 'push'?
TypeError list has no field 'length' — V2 writes len(x)
TypeError list has no method 'includes' — V2 writes item in x
TypeError list has no method 'forEach' — V2 loops with for item in x { ... }
TypeError str has no method 'toUpperCase' — did you mean 'upper'?
TypeError str has no method 'strip' — did you mean 'trim'?
TypeError str has no method 'startsWith' — did you mean 'starts_with'?
TypeError dict has no method 'items' — V2 loops over a dict with for key, value in d { ... }
TypeError dict has no method 'has' — V2 writes key in d
TypeError dict has no method 'pop' — did you mean 'remove'?
TypeError list has no method 'uppr'
NameError 'open' is not declared — V2 reads a file with read_file(path) and writes one with write_file(path, text)
NameError 'sorted' is not declared — V2 sorts a list with xs.sort()
TypeError str has no method 'join' — V2 joins a list with xs.join(sep)
ArityError error() needs a type and a message, as in error("ValueError", "my error"); throw "my error" throws a plain Error
NameError 'process' is not declared — V2 gets the script's arguments with args() and prints without a newline with print(x, end: "")
NameError 'sys' is not declared — V2 gets the script's arguments with args() and stops with exit(n); a Python module is imported with @import py.sys as sys
NameError 'Math' is not declared — V2 has min, max, abs, round, sum and div(a, b) built in; JavaScript's Math works in a @js block
NameError 'JSON' is not declared — V2 reads JSON with json_parse(text) and writes it with json_stringify(value)
NameError 'os' is not declared — V2 has getenv(name), list_dir(path), exists(path) and exec([...]) built in; a Python module is imported with @import py.os as os
NameError 'env' is not declared — V2 reads an environment variable with getenv(name)
